Hi Anbunithi, as discussed, we need your confirmation on the certificate approach we are following for CRM Olympus.

For each environment (DEV/UAT/PROD), we raise a CMP request and receive the certificate artifacts through CMP, including the PFX/certificate/private key. We then import the PFX into a JKS keystore using keytool.

In the application, we configure this generated JKS as the server.ssl.key-store. The JKS password/key password is encrypted using our application’s Jasypt configuration, and the encrypted value is maintained in the application properties instead of the plain-text password.

So our current flow is:
CMP request → PFX/certificate received → PFX imported into JKS → JKS configured in CRM Olympus → encrypted keystore/key password configured → deploy and validate.

Could you please confirm whether this is the correct/recommended approach? Also, please let us know if your application follows the same CMP certificate process or if any additional steps/configuration are required before we proceed with the remaining deployments.










import org.jasypt.encryption.pbe.PooledPBEStringEncryptor;
import org.jasypt.encryption.pbe.config.SimpleStringPBEConfig;

public class JasyptCheck {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Use the SAME CRM Olympus master password you used in the decrypt test
        String masterPassword = "YOUR_EXISTING_CRM_MASTER_PASSWORD";

        // New CMP/JKS password
        String plainPassword = "Olympusapicrmtoolympus1";

        PooledPBEStringEncryptor encryptor =
                new PooledPBEStringEncryptor();

        SimpleStringPBEConfig config =
                new SimpleStringPBEConfig();

        config.setPassword(masterPassword);
        config.setAlgorithm("PBEWITHHMACSHA512ANDAES_256");
        config.setKeyObtentionIterations("1000");
        config.setPoolSize("1");
        config.setSaltGeneratorClassName(
                "org.jasypt.salt.RandomSaltGenerator");
        config.setIvGeneratorClassName(
                "org.jasypt.iv.RandomIvGenerator");
        config.setStringOutputType("base64");

        encryptor.setConfig(config);

        String encrypted =
                encryptor.encrypt(plainPassword);

        System.out.println("ENC(" + encrypted + ")");
    }
}



        
        








